# The entry names every place: `run` hands `join` three paths, so the files it reads and writes are those files, each
# a place of its own (rule 5: a place a caller makes whole is touched where that caller is on the calls that lead
# there). `read_pair` reads both and gives a str, of no type of the code's, back to `join`, which writes it.

route storage.run
step run/join
step run/join/read_pair

line entry > run call
line File(data/first.txt) > run/join/read_pair own
line File(data/second.txt) > run/join/read_pair own
line run/join/read_pair > run/join back
line run/join > File(out/combined.txt) own

side entry left
side File(data/first.txt) left
side File(data/second.txt) left
side File(out/combined.txt) right
